{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments","id":1103397,"title":"Reaper mechanics: Using Souls without any specific legacy attainments.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T23:43:17-07:00","id":1103397,"title":"Reaper mechanics: Using Souls without any specific legacy attainments.","content":"The section on Reapers in MTA 2nd edition makes it sound as if Mages can accrue a wide variety of potent benefits from (mis)using captive souls, even without having attainments tied to a specific Reaper Legacy like the Tremere or Cloud Infinite. To quote &quot;Souls are incredibly powerful. A mage can consume a soul to access any of the Subtle Arcana that relate to her victim. She may drink deep on the Fated good fortune of one victim, and the intelligence and wits of another unwilling donor\u2019s Mind. She can also use a victim\u2019s soul to bind his ghost to her power, gaining his ghost as a slave to her will. She can even drain his soul to extend her own lifespan.&quot;<br /> <br /> I really like this idea of stolen souls being a very immediate and potent source of power for Mages, all the better to tempt your players into falling off the path of Wisdom! To me, soultheft being a very powerful practice seems good for the game. It helps explain why so many Mages might be tempted by such Left Handed practices in a way that the usually quite minor benefits laid out in 1st edition didn't. <br /> <br /> In any case here's some very rough back of a fag packet mechanics for such things that came to me while I should have been asleep last night. Commentary is welcome.<br /> <br /> By using a soul as a Yantra, a Mage can cast spells of <b>any </b>of the Subtle Arcana even if he does not have any dots in the Arcanum. Using a Soul this way does terrible damage to it, and repeated use will destroy it. <br /> <br /> Souls retain the Integrity/Wisdom Score of the person from whom the Soul has been taken from. Using the soul in this way degrades the Integrity/Wisdom score by a number of points equal to the dot level of the spell cast. This is an Act of Hubris against Understanding Wisdom, while using up the last point of Integrity (and destroying the soul) is against Falling Wisdom. I imagine many Reaper Legacies include attainments that allow you a way around the Wisdom effects.<br /> <br /> The dot level of spell the Reaper can cast is still limited by their Gnosis cap on highest Arcana. For example the Reaper could only use a soul to cast a 5 dot spell if they had a Gnosis of 5. <br /> <br /> All thoughts are welcome!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T00:10:12-07:00","id":1103402,"title":"","content":"Using a soul as a Yantra makes it a Sacrament and invariably destroys it. They typically act as a +2 Yantra for a subtle arcana spell, but you have to have the arcana in question.<br /> <br /> Not sure if you were actually aware of this or are making up something new so I'm letting you know.<br /> <br /> Even if you're just adding stuff, I wouldn't recommend letting players cast spells from arcana they don't have. That's just personal preference though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T07:30:20-07:00","id":1103477,"title":"","content":"Personally one thing I'd allow is to destroy a soul in order to safely relinquish a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T08:00:53-07:00","id":1103494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103477#post1103477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally one thing I'd allow is to destroy a soul in order to safely relinquish a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just 1 Willpower dot, or 1 XP.<br /> <br /> Hmm. I suppose burning the soul for a point of Paradox-free Reach would be too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T11:54:05-07:00","id":1103569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103494#post1103494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just 1 Willpower dot, or 1 XP.<br /> <br /> Hmm. I suppose burning the soul for a point of Paradox-free Reach would be too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not allow devouring a soul to automatically control of a Paradox Reach as the mage sees fit, as per the Scelesti mechanics, but without a roll instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T12:22:37-07:00","id":1103578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103569#post1103569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not allow devouring a soul to automatically control of a Paradox Reach as the mage sees fit, as per the Scelesti mechanics, but without a roll instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixes the two? Reapers are about souls, and Scelesti are about the Abyss(Paradox) and this would be mixing them? Why would a soul grant control over Paradox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-14-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T12:33:45-07:00","id":1103583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103494#post1103494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just 1 Willpower dot, or 1 XP.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and if you are willing to destroy a soul you can bypass the damage to your own psyche, making this an extremly tempting tradeoff.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:06:06-07:00","id":1103586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103583#post1103583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and if you are willing to destroy a soul you can bypass the damage to your own psyche, making this an extremly tempting tradeoff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Destroying a soul is a an AoH of Falling Wisdom, the cost of Wisdom is 2 XP. The numbers don't work out favorably for destroying souls to save on 1 XP and risk actually costing yourself 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:47:32-07:00","id":1103600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103586#post1103586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Destroying a soul is a an AoH of Falling Wisdom, the cost of Wisdom is 2 XP. The numbers don't work out favorably for destroying souls to save on 1 XP and risk actually costing yourself 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're telling me risking those 2 XP for a +2 Yantra is worth it, but gambling on effectivly skimming one xp wouldn't be? And of course risks like that are why reaper legacies are a thing, amongst other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:52:09-07:00","id":1103603,"title":"","content":"For Souls to be relevant I believe the power they offer and the risks they pose to Wisdom should be substantial. +2 Yantra is a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:02:40-07:00","id":1103607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103600#post1103600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're telling me risking those 2 XP for a +2 Yantra is worth it, but gambling on effectivly skimming one xp wouldn't be? And of course risks like that are why reaper legacies are a thing, amongst other reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're creating a false comparison, I didn't say that I thought a +2 Yantra was a good enough benefit to be worth the risk of 2 XP from buying back lost Wisdom. I was specifically talking to your suggestion as not being good enough in my opinion. In other words it's also inadequate.<br /> <br /> On another note, if you've Inured a spell then using a soul as a Sacrament on that spell means still no Wisdom risk I imagine. So that's a &quot;positive.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:19:57-07:00","id":1103614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103578#post1103578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mixes the two? Reapers are about souls, and Scelesti are about the Abyss(Paradox) and this would e mixing them? Why would a should grant control over Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gasoline can run an engine, or it can burn down a church. It can also be used as a solvent or a variety of other uses, technically. Potent and versatile fuels have a variety of properties and that's how souls are presented, as a potent versatile fuel.<br /> <br /> My soul using Scelesti'd be like a firetruck that sprays gasoline on churches, it has an engine and burns churches.<br /> <br /> A normal Reaper may &quot;merely&quot; be an engine in a monster truck that crushes other cars.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd be more surprised if there were a lack of abyssal applications to consuming souls than if there were a plethora of abyssal uses for such a fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-14-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:38:19-07:00","id":1103625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103603#post1103603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Souls to be relevant I believe the power they offer and the risks they pose to Wisdom should be substantial. +2 Yantra is a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Yantra that can be applied to any spell from half the Arcana without further regard for semiotics is nothing to sneeze at and the list of Yantras that give a higher bonus than +2 is very short. This is something you use to push your limits, not to fuel your basic spellwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T10:37:14-07:00","id":1103855,"title":"","content":"+2 isn't much. It's one level of Potency or Duration. Easy to Reach for plenty of Duration, so really +1 Potency for burning a Soul and risking Wisdom loss. Pretty crap IMO.<br /> <br /> Now, a Soul allowing you to double the Ritual time allowing for +10 is a different story.<br /> <br /> No PC in their right mind would ever destroy a Soul for +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 06-15-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T13:10:09-07:00","id":1103890,"title":"","content":"As a point of reference, the Nagaraja Legacy from Dark Eras uses Soul Jars as Yantras. When storing a Sleeper Soul, they're worth +1. When storing an Awakened Soul, they're worth +2. The book doesn't mention their value as Sacraments, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T13:37:36-07:00","id":1103902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103397-reaper-mechanics-using-souls-without-any-specific-legacy-attainments?p=1103855#post1103855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+2 isn't much. It's one level of Potency or Duration. Easy to Reach for plenty of Duration, so really +1 Potency for burning a Soul and risking Wisdom loss. Pretty crap IMO.<br /> <br /> Now, a Soul allowing you to double the Ritual time allowing for +10 is a different story.<br /> <br /> No PC in their right mind would ever destroy a Soul for +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could and might if they're casting an Inured spell, no Wisdom risk. They also would if they're invested in a legacy that regularly steals and uses souls, because at that point it's probably not an AoH for that Mage anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T14:40:53-07:00","id":1103945,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, but not much temptation otherwise really, which is my main beef.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb